ooc/docs:
=========

This directory contains various documents describing the OCT system.
The *.ro are the formatter output files, and are of the form
<char><BACKSPACE><char>.  To print on a dot matrix printer (without
beating the printhead to death), you should pipe them thru 'deroff'
which create <line><CR><line> formats.

The misc sub-directory are items collected about object-oriented
programming from various sources.

A whole bunch of neat articles written by Ed Benard are available
from a mailserver on  {uunet | unisoft.com } seer.UUCP.  The postmaster
will provide information about obtaining these informative USENET
postings.

--- brian witt, 8-Nov-90
